# Local chat model for `fleet-chat`: qwen3:4b with a bigger context window.
#
# Ollama runs models with a 4096-token context by default, and its OpenAI-compatible
# API (used by Pydantic AI) ignores per-request `num_ctx`.  9 tool schemas plus a few
# tool results do not fit in 4096 tokens; Ollama would silently drop the beginning of
# the conversation, including the instructions.  This derived model shares the
# weights of qwen3:4b (no extra download), only the default context changes.
#
# Create once:  ollama pull qwen3:4b && ollama create fleet-qwen3-4b -f Modelfile
#
# Why qwen3:4b (see README, "Chat model comparison"): it passed as many eval questions
# as qwen3:8b at half the size.  Measured on an RTX 4070 Laptop (8 GB): 4.5 GB with this
# context, 100 % on the GPU; qwen3:8b needed 15 % on the CPU at the same context.
# It uses the most context of the tested models (peak 9.2k of 12k in the eval), so keep
# 12288; with more VRAM, raise num_ctx for longer conversations.
FROM qwen3:4b
PARAMETER num_ctx 12288
